## Model card (identity resolution)

- **Name:** Omi Alpha (`omi-alpha`) — **no released AI model matches this name.** The two real "Omi/OMI" organizations in AI both fail to produce it:
  1. **Omi (omi.me, the AI wearable company)** — sells hardware (Omi DevKit 2, $89 pendant) that *routes* to third-party LLMs; its open-source platform captures/transcribes conversations and delegates inference to external models. No foundation model named "Alpha" (or any name) has been released; its app/model stack is not benchmarked as an "Omi Alpha" anywhere.
  2. **OMI — the Open Model Initiative (Linux Foundation, welcomed 2024-08-12)** — announced plans to "release an alpha version of a new model with fine-tuning scripts before the end of 2024" (Phoronix, InfoWorld, ITSFOSS, Linux Magazine). **That alpha model never shipped**: the project's current scope (openmodel.foundation, GitHub, LF AI & Data pages) is openly-licensed **image, video and audio generation** baselines, with no LLM release, no weights, and no benchmarks on record.
- **Provider / access:** none — no Hugging Face repo, no OpenRouter id, no API platform listing, no GitHub model release found for `omi-alpha`.
- **Release / knowledge:** n/a — never released.
- **IDs:** none found.
- **Context window:** n/a.
- **Modalities:** n/a.
- **Pricing:** n/a.
- **Architecture:** n/a.

